	# the Council (policy.gd, config/policies.json)
	"Way of life": "生存之道",
	"How the tribe feeds itself: what the Steward sends people to, and which work they grow good at.": "部落如何养活自己：管家派人去做什么，大家又擅长哪种活计。",
	"Foragers": "采集者",
	"Berries, roots and the gifts of the land. Gatherers favour bushes and finds over the hunt.": "浆果、根茎与大地的馈赠。采集者优先去灌木丛和发现物，而不是狩猎。",
	"The bushes do not bite back. We eat, and we live.": "灌木不会反咬人。我们有得吃，就能活。",
	"Berries! Are we birds? The herds are out there for the taking.": "浆果！我们是鸟吗？兽群就在那儿等着我们去拿。",
	"Hunters": "猎人",
	"The herds feed us. Gatherers go after deer first, and hunt better; but the hunt is dangerous.": "兽群养活我们。采集者先去追鹿，猎得更好；但狩猎很危险。",
	"Meat makes strong arms. Let the young ones learn the spear.": "吃肉才有力气。让年轻人学会用矛。",
	"Every hunt, someone comes back bleeding. Or does not come back.": "每次打猎，总有人流着血回来。或者再也回不来。",
	"Tillers": "耕种者",
	"We plant and wait. Fields give more; walking far for food matters less.": "我们播种，然后等待。田地产出更多，不必再远行觅食。",
	"A field remembers us. Plant once, eat many times.": "田地记得我们。种一次，吃很多回。",
	"Tied to the dirt like a stake in the ground. Is this how our fathers lived?": "像木桩一样钉在泥土里。我们的先辈是这样活的吗？",
	"Herders": "牧人",
	"The aurochs are our wealth: pens give more, and loads are lighter on the long walks.": "原牛是我们的财富：牛栏产出更多，远行时担子也更轻。",
	"A tame beast is food that walks to us.": "驯服的野兽，是自己走到我们身边的食物。",
	"Beasts to feed, beasts to tend. Who tends us?": "要喂牲口，要照料牲口。谁来照料我们？",
	"The forest": "森林",
	"How much the tribe takes from the trees.": "部落从树林里取用多少。",
	"Take only dead wood": "只取枯木",
	"The forest grows back quickly, but wood comes slower.": "森林长得快，但木材来得慢。",
	"The trees are old spirits. Take what they drop, and they keep giving.": "树是古老的精灵。拿它们掉下的，它们就会一直给予。",
	"Twigs will not raise huts.": "细枝盖不起小屋。",
	"Fell freely": "随意砍伐",
	"Cut what we need. The forest grows back at its own pace.": "需要多少就砍多少。森林按自己的步调长回来。",
	"We need wood; the forest has wood.": "我们需要木头，森林里有木头。",
	"We take and take.": "我们一直拿，一直拿。",
	"Burn to clear": "烧林开荒",
	"Fire opens the land: wood comes fast and fields grow on the ash, but the forest is slow to return and fires spread easily.": "火能开辟土地：木材来得快，灰烬上庄稼长得好；但森林恢复得慢，火也容易蔓延。",
	"The smoke of the burning hangs over the land. The elders look away.": "烧林的烟笼罩着大地。长老们别过脸去。",
	"Fire is the tribe's servant. Let it clear the way.": "火是部落的仆人。让它为我们开路。",
	"Fire has no master. One dry wind and it eats our huts too.": "火没有主人。一阵干风，它连我们的小屋也会吞掉。",
	"The hunt": "狩猎",
	"Which beasts the hunters may take.": "猎人可以猎取哪些野兽。",
	"Spare the mothers": "放过母兽",
	"Hunt less, but the herds grow back strong.": "少猎一些，兽群却能兴旺起来。",
	"Kill the mother, and next spring there is no calf.": "杀了母兽，明年春天就没有小崽。",
	"A hungry belly does not ask which deer it was.": "饿肚子可不管是哪头鹿。",
	"Hunt what comes": "遇到什么猎什么",
	"Take any beast. The herds come back as they will.": "什么野兽都猎。兽群自会回来。",
	"The herds are many.": "兽群多得很。",
	"The herds are fewer every year.": "兽群一年比一年少。",
	"Hunt everything": "赶尽杀绝",
	"More meat now; fewer herds later.": "眼下肉多，往后兽少。",
	"Every deer we leave, a wolf eats.": "我们留下的每头鹿，都会被狼吃掉。",
	"When the plains are empty, what will our children hunt?": "等草原空了，我们的孩子猎什么？",
	"The spirits we honour": "我们敬奉的神灵",
	"Whom the tribe turns to: what its rituals bring and what it becomes.": "部落向谁祈求：仪式带来什么，部落又将成为什么样子。",
	"The ancestors": "祖先",
	"The dead watch over us: lore comes more easily and the tribe takes comfort in its past.": "逝者守护着我们：学识来得更容易，部落从过往中得到慰藉。",
	"Those who came before us still walk beside us.": "先我们而去的人，仍走在我们身旁。",
	"The dead are dead. The living need food.": "死了就是死了。活人需要吃的。",
	"The sky": "天空",
	"Sun, storm and stars: the cold bites less, and rituals bring more devotion.": "太阳、风暴与星辰：寒冷不那么刺骨，仪式带来更多虔诚。",
	"The sky sends rain and lightning both. Better it knows our names.": "天降雨水，也降雷电。最好让它记住我们的名字。",
	"The sky does not listen. It never has.": "天不会听。它从来没听过。",
	"The beast spirits": "兽灵",
	"The tiger, the aurochs, the great serpent: hunters strike harder and the hunt goes better.": "猛虎、原牛、巨蛇：猎手出手更狠，狩猎更顺。",
	"Wear the tiger's strength, and the tiger fears you.": "披上猛虎的力量，猛虎就会怕你。",
	"Call the beasts, and the beasts may come.": "呼唤野兽，野兽也许真会来。",
	"What to seek": "求知方向",
	"Where the tribe's curiosity goes: which ideas grow faster from everyday work.": "部落的好奇心投向哪里：哪些想法会从日常劳作中更快萌发。",
	"Whatever comes": "顺其自然",
